From: PromethenDev <PromethenDev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 07:18:22 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 86/97] Window: cursor auto-hide on Linux (GTK) and a 4 s delay

GTKWindow now implements CursorVisibility (kVisible / kHidden / kAutoHidden): in auto-hide the pointer over the game
area is hidden after kDefaultCursorAutoHideMilliseconds without real mouse movement, clicks or scrolling, and shown
again on the next one (synthetic motion events with an unchanged position are ignored). The timer is removed when the
window closes. kDefaultCursorAutoHideMilliseconds 3333 -> 4000 (Windows uses the same value).
---
 include/rex/ui/window.h     |  2 +-
 include/rex/ui/window_gtk.h | 12 ++++++
 src/ui/window_gtk.cpp       | 78 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 91 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/rex/ui/window.h b/include/rex/ui/window.h
index 4bf2d7c..aceeade 100644
--- a/include/rex/ui/window.h
+++ b/include/rex/ui/window.h
@@ -415,7 +415,7 @@ class Window {
   // but it's too long especially for highly dynamic games.
   // Implementations may use different values according to the platform's UX
   // conventions.
-  static constexpr uint32_t kDefaultCursorAutoHideMilliseconds = 3333;
+  static constexpr uint32_t kDefaultCursorAutoHideMilliseconds = 4000;
 
   Window(WindowedAppContext& app_context, const std::string_view title,
          uint32_t desired_logical_width, uint32_t desired_logical_height);
diff --git a/include/rex/ui/window_gtk.h b/include/rex/ui/window_gtk.h
index 433fda3..f78fd27 100644
